<h2>JavaScript Standard Style rules</h2>
<hr>
<p>These are a collection of the more "prevalent" style rules. For more detailed information and examples, please refer to
  <a href="https://standardjs.com/rules.html" target='_blank' rel='noreferrer'>JavaScript Standard Style's documentation</a>.
  <ul>
    <li>Use 2 spaces for indentation.</li>
    <li>Use 'single quotes' for strings except to avoid escaping e.g. <code>"It's"</code> instead of <code>'It\'s'</code>.</li>
    <li>Do not leave unused variables in code.</li>
    <li>Add a space after keywords e.g. <code>if (condition) { ... }</code> instead of <code>if(condition){ ... }</code>.</li>
    <li>Always use <code>===</code> instead of <code>==</code>.</li>
    <li>Infix operators must be spaced e.g. <code>1 + 1</code> instead of <code>1+1</code>.</li>
    <li>Commas should have a space after them.</li>
  </ul>
</p>
